# Nginx answers robot probes

This storefront must answer `/robots.txt` and `/sitemap.xml` inside Nginx. Keep these locations in `deploy/nginx-ngo.conf` on port 80 and port 443, and in `deploy/nginx-ngo-http.conf`, placed before `location /`. Change only `server_name` via `__SITE_DOMAIN__` in those templates.

```
location = /robots.txt {
    default_type text/plain;
    add_header Cache-Control "public, max-age=86400" always;
    return 200 "User-agent: *\nDisallow: /\n";
}

location = /sitemap.xml {
    default_type application/xml;
    add_header Cache-Control "public, max-age=86400" always;
    return 200 "<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?><urlset xmlns=\"http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9\"></urlset>\n";
}
```

`deploy/apply-ngo-vps.sh` installs `nginx-ngo.conf` when the certificate exists and `nginx-ngo-http.conf` until then, so both files need the locations. Do not send these paths to Node.
